WEBVTT

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:03.860
Local and private AI shift responsibility toward the organization.

00:00:03.860 --> 00:00:08.060
Teams may gain control over data flow, model selection, and runtime behavior,

00:00:08.060 --> 00:00:10.220
but they also own more of the infrastructure.

00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:16.145
GPUs, CPUs, memory, storage, model caches, vector stores, backups, networking, queues,

00:00:16.145 --> 00:00:17.795
scheduling, monitoring, patching,

00:00:17.795 --> 00:00:20.515
and recovery planning all become part of the operating model.

00:00:20.515 --> 00:00:22.825
Cost drivers can be easy to underestimate.

00:00:22.825 --> 00:00:27.480
Accelerator time, idle resources, storage for model files, embeddings, logs, backups,

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:30.535
data movement, monitoring systems, and staff time all matter.

00:00:30.535 --> 00:00:34.740
A private system that appears inexpensive during a pilot can become expensive when many

00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:35.170
users,

00:00:35.170 --> 00:00:39.260
large context windows, multiple models, and retained telemetry enter the picture.

00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:42.660
Reliability matters because useful AI systems attract real work.

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:46.820
Once people depend on the platform, downtime, slow responses, missing indexes,

00:00:46.820 --> 00:00:50.965
stale documents, failed backups, and unclear ownership become business problems.

00:00:50.965 --> 00:00:55.300
Resource limits, usage tracking, cleanup routines, model cache management, queue controls,

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:58.725
and shutdown policies help prevent uncontrolled growth and surprise costs.

00:00:58.725 --> 00:01:01.820
A sovereign AI environment should include backup and restore plans,

00:01:01.820 --> 00:01:06.120
configuration management, capacity planning, incident ownership, and recovery procedures.

00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:08.920
It should also define what happens when a local node fails,

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:14.030
a model endpoint is unavailable, an index is corrupted, or a cost threshold is exceeded.

00:01:14.030 --> 00:01:17.720
Infrastructure decisions should support the workflow without creating fragile operations

00:01:17.720 --> 00:01:19.480
that only one person understands.

00:01:19.480 --> 00:01:22.285
Operational planning should be tied to real usage patterns.

00:01:22.285 --> 00:01:26.600
Track which teams use which models, when demand spikes, which collections grow fastest,

00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:27.700
and where requests queue.

00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:31.660
That evidence supports right-sized hardware, cleanup work, and budget conversations.

00:01:31.660 --> 00:01:36.540
Sovereignty is easier to sustain when cost and reliability are visible before they become

00:01:36.540 --> 00:01:36.720
surprises.
